Three crates.io packages are built from forks with small changes of our own, taken as git
dependencies pinned by commit in Cargo.toml (see docs/dev/development.md, "Форки
сторонних крейтов"). Each change is a signed commit in the branch of the fork named
below; the branch starts at the upstream commit the package was published from.

i-slint-backend-winit 1.18.1 is part of Slint (https://slint.dev), Copyright SixtyFPS
GmbH, used under the Slint Royalty-free Desktop, Mobile, and Web Applications License 2.0
(see the LICENSES directory of the package). The fork is
https://github.com/arynyklas/slint, branch openncalayer/i-slint-backend-winit-1.18.1,
from https://github.com/slint-ui/slint commit 372cf0ee5577c3dfec309a45e7b778ba4e81b734
(internal/backends/winit). It is modified: on Windows, lib.rs looks up
SystemParametersInfoForDpi at run time and falls back to SystemParametersInfoW instead
of importing it, and Cargo.toml enables the Win32_System_LibraryLoader feature of the
windows crate; the internal Slint crates and vtable are declared by version instead of
by path, and the licence texts are files instead of symlinks.

velopack 1.3.39-g8d2844f is Velopack (https://github.com/velopack/velopack), Copyright
(c) 2021 Caelan Sayler and (c) 2024 Velopack Ltd., distributed under the MIT License
(see src/lib-rust/LICENSE of the fork, a copy of the repository's licence file; the
crates.io package ships none). The fork is https://github.com/arynyklas/velopack, branch
openncalayer/velopack-1.3.39-g8d2844f, from commit
8d2844f324a69bd848719ef465b1ae12c5060524. It is modified: src/sources/mod.rs adds the
UpdateSource::verify_full_package hook (its default is Velopack's own size and checksum
check), and src/manager.rs (download_updates) checks with it a full package already on
disk before skipping the download, deleting one that fails, and a package rebuilt from
deltas before it is renamed into place and Squirrel.exe is extracted from it, falling
back to the full download when it fails; the crate carries the published version.

multer 3.1.0 is https://github.com/rwf2/multer (commit
09cc7300c9bb7b3bbb30776e87ce14d2bd85588f), Copyright (c) 2020 Rousan Ali, distributed
under the MIT License (see its LICENSE). The fork is https://github.com/arynyklas/multer,
branch openncalayer/multer-3.1.0. It adds an optional observer of the raw multipart
framing bytes, without changing how the existing parser reads them, and checks the stream
size counter for overflow.

crates/oncl-gost/src/streebog_secret.rs and crates/oncl-gost/src/streebog_secret/consts.rs
are derived from streebog 0.11.0, a RustCrypto crate (https://github.com/RustCrypto/hashes,
commit b5051e5a5e7dc86a6c27c1ec7a390744ebcfb97a), Copyright (c) 2016-2026 The RustCrypto
Project Developers and Copyright (c) 2016 Artyom Pavlov, distributed under the MIT or
Apache-2.0 licenses and used here under Apache-2.0. consts.rs is a verbatim copy. The
secret-input Streebog was first kept in a fork (https://github.com/arynyklas/hashes, branch
openncalayer/streebog-0.11.0, commit 7f67647379b26e89068874cfe8cf3bf0c8e72b69) and is now
part of oncl-gost. It is modified: the LPS step selects the table words with constant-time
selection (the subtle crate) instead of loading them at secret indexes, the compression
temporaries live in one workspace wiped after every block, the state is one heap allocation
made before any input, and the state is wiped as soon as the digest is written.
crates/oncl-gost/src/secret_hmac.rs is our own RFC 2104 HMAC over it, in place of a former
fork of hmac 0.13.0 (https://github.com/arynyklas/MACs, branch openncalayer/hmac-0.13.0).
Public documents, PKCS#12 and PBKDF2 use the unmodified crates.io streebog and hmac. These
changes are not an upstream certification or a blanket constant-time guarantee for every
compiler, target or build profile.

The SDK packages (oncl-core and its dependency chain, docs/dev/sdk.md) each carry LICENSE
and a NOTICE of their own; crates/oncl-core/THIRD-PARTY.txt lists the third-party crates of
the SDK closure with their licence texts (generated by `cargo xtask sdk licenses`).
crates/oncl-pki/roots/ contains the public production CA certificates of the National
Certification Authority of the Republic of Kazakhstan (copies of fixtures/nca/prod); the
rights to those certificates belong to their issuer and are not licensed under Apache-2.0.
